  "term": "Alfenta",
  "definition": "Alfenta is the hydrochloride form of alfentanil, a synthetic short-acting opioid. It mainly acts at mu-opioid receptors to produce pain-relieving effects similar to morphine and can reduce the release of several neurotransmitters and hormones.",
